  "id": "bispf-settling-displacement-v1",
  "mechanism_class": "structural",
  "mechanism_rationale": "Pre-normalization thermal scaling can leave the magnitude of a normalized finite update nearly unchanged above optimizer smoothing. Applying the same earned thermal signal to the actual combined generator/prior displacement makes its finite velocity responsive without an idle threshold, a moment-force cap or a time schedule. Restoring the uncooled generator and SBNP objective gradients before normalization avoids double cooling and preserves a declared common objective direction; this is one combined cooling-location mechanism. The existing observer still reheats under increased residual. Unchanged Gaussian/overlap gates and protected controls must decide whether this settles the model without sacrificing acquisition or target-shift response; no qualification or default-adoption claim.",
